          "content": "#### Additional resources\n**Insights for Executives**\n- Increase operational efficiency with automation and AI to foster seamless collaboration\n- Unify tools to eliminate redundancies, rein in costs, and ease compliance\n- Break data silos and add context for faster, more strategic decisions\n- Minimize security risks by reducing complexity with unified observability\n- Simplify data ingestion and up-level storage for better, faster querying\n**Blog posts**\n* [Unified observability is key to consolidating tool sprawl and breaking down data silos](https://www.dynatrace.com/news/blog/unified-observability-key-to-consolidating-tool-sprawl/)\n* [Cut costs and complexity: 5 strategies for reducing tool sprawl with Dynatrace](https://www.dynatrace.com/news/blog/dynatrace-for-executives-tool-sprawl/)\n**Account Team**\n* Consult your Account Team to get appropriate support on your tool consolidation strategy\n#\n---\n\n#### About this dashboard\n\n**User access**\n\n* This dashboard uses data in `dt.entity.process_group_instance` and `user.events` tables about running processes and RUM events. Adapt IAM policies depending on the authorization or restriction to give to users.\n\n**Accuracy**\n* Although the matching of alternative agents can neither be fully exhaustive (eg. because of custom agent process names) nor exempt from a few false positives, the 150+ detection patterns leveraged in this dashboard have been thoroughly crafted and get regularly updated for maximum precision.\n\n\n**Query optimization**\n* Depending on the volume behind the user events table, it may reach the defined limit of 1TB of data scanned. To expand the coverage of the frontend agent detection, it's possible to uplift this query limit (see [Query scan limit](https://docs.dynatrace.com/docs/platform/grail/dynatrace-query-language/dql-best-practices#further-options-to-limit-the-scanned-amount-of-data)).\n\nRelease v1.4",
